One more axiom naturally follows from yours:

Every translation is a hypothesis about what matters.

A translator, compiler, or scientist is always making a choice about which properties to preserve. That makes translation itself an epistemic act, not just a mechanical one.

Then the loop becomes:

Choose invariant
      ↓
Translate
      ↓
Measure preservation
      ↓
Revise the invariant if necessary

Notice that the invariant isn’t sacred—it can itself be revised if repeated translations reveal that you were preserving the wrong thing.

